      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Bright or dark",
      "body": "A major triad sounds bright and open, a minor triad sounds darker and more serious. Only the 3rd differs, so listen to the middle note.\n\n**Why it matters:** when you play by ear, the first thing to work out about a chord is major or minor. Get that and the root, and you have the chord.",
